{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "1997-04-02T00:00:00+00:00", "metadata": {"publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "56", "page_end": "5557", "year": 1997, "page_start": "5524", "journal_title": "Phys.Rev.D"}], "authors": [{"full_name": "Radyushkin, A.V."}], "texkeys": ["Radyushkin:1997ki"], "abstracts": [{"value": "Applications of perturbative QCD to deeply virtual Compton scattering and hard exclusive electroproduction processes require a generalization of usual parton distributions for the case when long-distance information is accumulated in nonforward matrix elements <p'|O|p> of quark and gluon light-cone operators. We describe two types of nonperturbative functions parametrizing such matrix elements: double distributions F(x,y;t) and nonforward distribution functions F_\\zeta (X;t), discuss their spectral properties, evolution equations which they satisfy, basic uses and general aspects of factorization for hard exclusive processes."}], "control_number": 441746, "dois": [{"value": "10.1103/PhysRevD.56.5524"}], "arxiv_eprints": [{"value": "hep-ph/9704207"}], "titles": [{"title": "Nonforward parton distributions"}, {"title": "Nonforward parton distributions."}, {"title": "Nonforward Parton Distributions"}], "author_count": 1, "document_type": ["article"]}, "id": "441746", "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/441746?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/441746?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/441746?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/441746?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/441746?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/441746?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A441746"}, "updated": "2026-06-15T13:40:34.465303+00:00"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=eprint%20hep-ph%2F9704207&size=3&